        "procedure": "Dy(NO3)3·5H2O (0.048 g, 0.11 mmol) was added to a methanol solution (30 mL) of H4L (0.040 g, 0.11 mmol) at room temperature, affording a yellow solution. Triethylamine (0.046 mL, 0.33 mmol) was added and the mixture was stirred overnight at room temperature. The solution was filtered and the filtrate was evaporated in vacuo to a yellow residue, which was dissolved in methanol (5 mL) and crystallized by slow evaporation. X-ray quality crystals formed within 3–4 days.",
