        "procedure": "Solid DyCl3·6H2O (0.082 g, 0.22 mmol) and H4L (0.040 g, 0.11 mmol) were taken in methanol (30 mL) and stirred for 5 min at room temperature. Tetrabutylammonium hydroxide (0.55 mmol) was added dropwise. After 15 min, pivalic acid (0.22 mmol) was added and the mixture was stirred for 8 h at room temperature. Volatiles were removed in vacuo to a semisolid yellow residue, which was dissolved in methanol (5 mL) and chloroform (2 mL) and crystallized by slow evaporation. Suitable crystals were harvested in 2–3 days.",
